### Cloud API tests (Lab 7, Part 3) - open in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension
### and click "Send Request" above each test.
### 1. Put your four API URLs below (bash infra/deploy-backend.sh all prints them,
###    or: source infra/gym-vars.sh && echo $IDENTITY_API_URL ...). No slash at the end.
### 2. Put the e-mail/password of a demo member (infra/.generated/seed-credentials.txt).

@identity = http://REPLACE.execute-api.localhost.floci.io:4566
@classes = http://REPLACE.execute-api.localhost.floci.io:4566
@bookings = http://REPLACE.execute-api.localhost.floci.io:4566
@attendance = http://REPLACE.execute-api.localhost.floci.io:4566
@memberEmail = ali.member@gym.local
@memberPassword = PASTE-FROM-seed-credentials.txt

### T1  Health: every API runs on Lambda  -> 200, "runtime":"lambda"
GET {{identity}}/api/health

###
GET {{classes}}/api/health

###
GET {{bookings}}/api/health

###
GET {{attendance}}/api/health

### T2  Sign in as a member -> 200 + accessToken (the next requests reuse it)
# @name login
POST {{identity}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{memberEmail}}", "password": "{{memberPassword}}" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### T3  Public timetable -> 200 + classes with live places
GET {{classes}}/api/classes

### T4  My bookings with the token -> 200
GET {{bookings}}/api/bookings/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### T5  Same request WITHOUT a token -> 401 UNAUTHENTICATED
GET {{bookings}}/api/bookings/mine

### T6  Invalid data -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED (short name, bad e-mail, weak password, extra field)
POST {{identity}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "X", "email": "not-an-email", "password": "short", "role": "admin" }

### T7  A member tries a trainer action -> 403 ROLE_NOT_ALLOWED
POST {{classes}}/api/classes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Hacked class", "category": "yoga", "studioId": "5e2a7c1e-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "startTime": "2030-01-01T08:00:00Z", "durationMin": 60, "capacity": 10 }

### T8  A route that is not in API Gateway -> 404 {"message":"Not Found"} (Lambda never runs)
DELETE {{identity}}/api/health

### T9  Internal endpoint from outside -> 404 from API Gateway (only reachable Lambda-to-Lambda)
POST {{bookings}}/internal/booking-counts
Content-Type: application/json

{ "classIds": [] }

### T10 CORS from our website -> Access-Control-Allow-Origin: http://localhost:4566
OPTIONS {{bookings}}/api/bookings
Origin: http://localhost:4566
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST

### T11 CORS from another site -> NO Access-Control-Allow-Origin header
OPTIONS {{bookings}}/api/bookings
Origin: https://evil.example
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST
